      "title": "Andy Burnham pressed on borrowing costs and spending at first PMQs – UK politics live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/02/pmqs-andy-burnham-kemi-badenoch-labour-uk-politics-latest-news",
      "description": "<p>Burnham faced questions from Kemi Badenoch and other MPs amid speculation over budget</p><p>In the news release to mark the first anniversary of his election as the Green party’s leader, <strong>Zack Polanski</strong> highlighted what he described as 10 achievements during his first year in charge. For the record, this is how he sees his record.</p><p>-Won the Greens’ first ever parliamentary byelection in Gorton and Denton</p><p>-More than tripled the party membership from 68,500 to over 230,000</p><p>Zack Polanski in Holborn and St Pancras sounds like a done deal from the hints the party is dropping over the past 24 hours. Needs the formality of local party sign-off.</p><p>Our budget for day-to-day spending next year will be lower in real terms than this year. Our capital budget will fall in real terms every year until the end of the decade.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/02/pmqs-andy-burnham-kemi-badenoch-labour-uk-politics-latest-news\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-02T15:19:37"
    },
    {
      "title": "Andy Burnham blames Tory legacy for leaving UK economy vulnerable",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/02/andy-burnham-blames-tory-legacy-uk-economy-vulnerable",
      "description": "<p>In first PMQs clash with Kemi Badenoch, prime minister rejects comparison to Liz Truss’s government</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/02/pmqs-andy-burnham-kemi-badenoch-labour-uk-politics-latest-news\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Andy Burnham blamed the Conservatives’ legacy for leaving the UK vulnerable to market turmoil, in his first prime ministers’ questions clash with Kemi Badenoch, as the UK’s borrowing costs climbed further.</p><p>The Conservative leader compared the market pressure on Burnham’s second day to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/oct/20/the-mini-budget-that-broke-britain-and-liz-truss\">Liz Truss’s mini-Budget</a>. But the prime minister said it was the Tories’ failure to address the UK’s growth and debt which meant the economy was exposed to market shocks.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/02/andy-burnham-blames-tory-legacy-uk-economy-vulnerable\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-02T13:30:51"
    }
